.TH MAKECRC 1.SH NAMEmakecrc \- generate C source for CRC tables.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmakecrc\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBmakecrc\fRwrites six C files into the current directory -- arc.c, binhex.c,ccitt.c, ccitt32.c, kermit.c and zip.c -- each holding a\fBcrctab[256]\fRand an\fBupdcrc()\fRfor one polynomial, for use in the macutils programs.  It takes noarguments and prints nothing, so list the directory afterwards.  Tocompute the CRC of a file, use\fBchksum\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOchksum